  "digitizer_notes": "Re-processed 2026-07-06 after user PASS/FAIL visual audit flagged a poor local fit on red_cyan_forming_layer around exposure -2.1 to -1.6, and 'messed up' curves below exposure -1.7. Root cause #1: the toe-vs-merged splice point (previously image col 380) sat right where the toe-specific 3-slot trace had a brief tracking wobble (cols 369-374) -- pulled the splice point in to col 365, and added an isolated-point filter, same fix class as Velvia 50 the same day. Root cause #2 (bigger): frame_bottom was wrongly set to image row 615, cutting off the real curve well before its true end -- direct pixel inspection confirmed the curve continues past row 615 all the way to the real frame bottom (~row 750); row 615 was mistaken for the y=0.0 gridline when it's actually an intermediate gridline further up. Corrected frame_bottom to 754, recovering the full real Dmin tail this was silently truncating. Curve identity re-confirmed by toe row order (Green highest, Blue middle, Red lowest). QA overlay: both a combined (all 3 curves) plot and one PNG per curve."
